# Story page: sunflower
# {name} becomes the snake's name. Paragraphs are separated by a blank line.
title = Sunflower Fields
---
Past the yard the grass grew gold, and the sunflowers stood so tall that {name} had to crane its whole body to see their faces.

Two apples hung in the warm air at once, which felt greedy, and a third gleamed golden, which felt like a trap. It was not. It was simply delicious, and the sun seemed to approve.

The more {name} ate, the warmer it felt, until it fairly glowed. I believe this is called a fever. I believe it is not, in this case, a medical problem, but I have been wrong about fevers before.
